    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass. The full suite contains one executable test class (`AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), which now passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n\n**How it works:** `membershipNumber` is purely derived from the owner's own fields (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`), so I computed it in the mapper alongside the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than persisting a redundant column \u2014 matching the codebase's existing pattern and the test's note that it's \"derived from the owner's own fields, so seed-independent.\"\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in the API response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `membershipNumber(owner)` helper that formats `customerCode + \"-M\" + <last two digits of registrationDate year>` (zero-padded, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), returning `null` when either source field is absent.\n\nThe `customerCode` (set at creation in `ClinicServiceImpl`) and `registrationDate` (defaulted to the current date in the controller) are both already populated, so the membership number resolves correctly on both create and fetch responses.",
